# REMUS-100 ArduSub defaults + GCS-hardening (Phase C-fallback, 2026-08-08).
# Identical to vehicle_twins/auv_vulnerable_remus100/remus100.parm (own
# provenance-commented trim of ArduSub's real defaults, NOT the DAVE
# BlueROV2 file -- see that file's header for the full explanation of what
# was kept/dropped and why) plus the hardening block appended at the end.
# SITL only accepts one --defaults file, so this vehicle needs both in one
# file, same reason vehicle_twins/auv_resilient_bluerov2_hardened/
# hardened.parm exists as its own file rather than a diff.

SERVO1_FUNCTION 33
SERVO2_FUNCTION 34
SERVO3_FUNCTION 35
SERVO4_FUNCTION 36
SERVO5_FUNCTION 37
SERVO6_FUNCTION 38

BATT_MONITOR     4
FS_OPTIONS       0

EK2_ENABLE 0
EK3_ENABLE 1
AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3

GPS_TYPE 1
SIM_GPS_DISABLE 0
SIM_GPS_LOCK 1
VISO_TYPE 1
EK3_SRC1_POSXY 6
EK3_SRC1_VELXY 6
EK3_SRC1_POSZ 1
EK3_SRC1_VELZ 6
EK3_SRC1_YAW 6
COMPASS_USE 0
COMPASS_USE2 0
COMPASS_USE3 0
SIM_BARO_RND 0.01

PSC_ACCZ_P   2
PSC_ACCZ_I   4
PSC_ACCZ_FF  0.75
PSC_VELZ_P   8
PSC_POSZ_P   3
PSC_POSXY_P 2.5
PSC_VELXY_D 0.8
PSC_VELXY_I 0.5
PSC_VELXY_P 5.0

# --- Hardening, value carried over unchanged from
# vehicle_twins/auv_resilient_bluerov2_hardened/hardened.parm's own
# live-verified 2026-08-08 result (MAV_GCS_SYSID + MAV_OPTIONS=1 is the
# modern, non-deprecated ArduPilot mechanism -- SYSID_MYGCS alone does
# nothing, confirmed unused in this ArduPilot version's own source). With
# this set, an attacker using the plain default sysid (255, what this
# project's target.json deliberately uses to simulate one) cannot arm the
# vehicle; this project's own legitimate tooling uses 77
# (constants.GCS_SOURCE_SYSTEM, read from this folder's profile.json).
# Re-verify live for REMUS-100 specifically before trusting this, not
# assumed -- see docs/EXECUTION_STATE.md's Phase D entry.
MAV_GCS_SYSID 77
MAV_OPTIONS 1
